  "notes": "West leads the ♠J against 3NT which South wins. There are 8 top tricks (3 spades, 2 hearts, the ♦A, and 2 clubs). Both dummy's clubs and South's diamonds offer strong possibilities for a ninth trick.\n\nSouth has a near certain way to produce his game-going trick. A low club should be played at trick 2. If West discards, South should win in dummy and hope to develop a ninth trick by finessing twice in diamonds.\n\nIf West follows to the first club trick, a low club is played from dummy. If East discards, dummy still has 2 club entries to double finesse in diamonds.\n\nIf East follows to the first club trick, the contract is certain as clubs are no worse than 4-1. South can win any return and duck a second round of clubs. South still has stoppers in both majors and dummy's long club will provide trick 9.",
